<h4>BufferBuddy Settings</h4>

<form class="form-horizontal" id="settings_plugin_buffer_buddy_form">
	<div class="control-group">
		<label class="control-label">
      {{ _('Enabled') }}
    </label>
		<div class="controls">
				<input type="checkbox" data-bind="checked: settings.plugins.buffer_buddy.enabled" title="If enabled, BufferBuddy will try to keep buffers full."/>
        <br />
        <small>If enabled, BufferBuddy will try to keep buffers full, otherwise it will monitor buffers only.</small>
		</div>
	</div>
  <div class="control-group">
		<label class="control-label">{{ _('Printer RX buffer size') }}</label>
		<div class="controls">
			<input type="number" min="48" max="65536" style="width: 6em" class="input-block-level" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.buffer_buddy.rx_buffer_size"></input> bytes
      <br />
      <small>
        Your firmware's `RX_BUFFER_SIZE` (Marlin's default is 128). Lines the printer hasn't read yet wait here, and if too many arrive at once the printer drops bytes and asks for a resend. Only raise it if your firmware's buffer is bigger.
      </small>
		</div>
	</div>
</form>